{"pr":211,"status":"fulfilled","value":{"chunk_id":"430145","wall_time_seconds":1.143924167,"exit_code":0,"original_token_count":1929,"output":"{\"body\": \"## Purpose\\n\\nCloses [EVO-16](https://linear.app/evorto/issue/EVO-16/require-sign-in-for-taxrateslistactive).\\n\\n`taxRates.listActive` only rejected signed-in callers without `templates:view`. An anonymous request skipped the check and received the tenant's active tax rates, including the Stripe tax-rate IDs. The handler now uses `RpcAccess.ensurePermission('templates:view')`, the guard the other permissioned handlers use.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- `src/server/effect/rpc/handlers/tax-rates.handlers.ts`: replace the custom check with `RpcAccess.ensurePermission('templates:view')`. Anonymous callers get `RpcUnauthorizedError`; signed-in callers without the permission still get `RpcForbiddenError` for `templates:view`, now with the shared message.\\n- `src/shared/rpc-contracts/app-rpcs/tax-rates.rpcs.ts`: the error schema becomes the existing `ForbiddenOrUnauthorizedRpcError`. Without it the handler no longer satisfies the contract (`TS2322`, checked with a focused `tsc` run), and the server could not encode the new error.\\n- `src/server/effect/rpc/handlers/tax-rates.handlers.spec.ts`: new case for an anonymous caller: `RpcUnauthorizedError` and no database read. It fails on `main` (the handler reads the tax rates) and passes with the fix. The forbidden, allowed and permission-dependency cases were already covered.\\n- `src/server/effect/rpc/handlers/platform/platform-event-creation.postgres.spec.ts`: this spec read the tenant catalog anonymously to compare it with `platform.events.formOptions`; it now uses a signed-in context with `templates:view`. The assertions are unchanged.\\n- Knope change file.\\n\\nNo schema, migration or UI change. Every app caller already requires a sign-in: the template pages sit behind `authGuard` (`src/app/app.routes.ts:23`), and event edit loads `events.findGraphForEdit`, which calls `RpcAccess.ensureAuthenticated()` (`src/server/effect/rpc/handlers/events/events-query.handlers.ts:543`). No public page calls this RPC.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nComplete local PR Quality gate on tree `7493b007` (commit `73c91337`), run in Docker with bun 1.4.2 and Node 24.22.1; the Chromium install and non-root test user match CI:\\n\\n- Frozen dependency install, Knope 0.23.0 validation, formatting and lint passed. Lint retains three existing unused-variable warnings in files this change does not touch.\\n- Server unit suite: 2,693 passed, 0 skipped.\\n- Application unit suite: 1,707 passed, 0 skipped.\\n- PostgreSQL integration suite: 383 passed, 0 skipped, against a disposable PostgreSQL 17.11 container. This includes the adjusted platform event-creation spec.\\n- Terraform formatting, validation of all three roots, and HIGH/CRITICAL configuration scanning passed.\\n- Docker build-context check, linux/amd64 production image build, runtime/size checks (96,299,570 bytes), private source-map export, SBOM, and HIGH/CRITICAL vulnerability scan passed.\\n- Red/green: the new anonymous-caller case fails on `main` (the handler reads the tax rates for an anonymous caller) and passes with the fix.\\n- A focused `tsc` run over the handler, its spec and the contract reports no errors; with the old `ForbiddenRpcError` contract it fails with `TS2322` on the handler.\\n\\n## Not verified\\n\\nThe Playwright baseline was not run: no page an anonymous visitor can open calls this RPC, and signed-in behavior is unchanged. I did not call the RPC over HTTP against a running stack, so the anonymous rejection is proven by the handler spec and the contract type, not on the wire.\\n\\n- `main` <!-- branch-stack -->\\n  - **EVO-16: Require sign-in for taxRates.listActive** :point\\\\_left:\\n\\n\\ud83e\\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\", \"comments\": [{\"id\": \"IC_kwDONgQCms8AAAABkCq4DA\", \"author\": {\"login\": \"linear-code\"}, \"authorAssoci